```comment
T1059.001 - PowerShell with an encoded command
```

```comment
SEARCH A (validated): Sysmon process creation, powershell.exe launched with an encoded-command flag.
Observed in lab: "-encodedcommand dwBoAG8AYQBtAGkA..." launched from powershell.exe by the local user.
```
index=sysmon EventCode=1 Image="*\\powershell.exe" (CommandLine="*-enc*" OR CommandLine="*-EncodedCommand*")
| table _time host User ParentImage CommandLine


```comment
SEARCH B (validated): PowerShell script block logging, EventCode 4104. Shows the DECODED content.
Add a keyword (here "whoami") to narrow to your test, or remove it to review all script blocks.
```
index=wineventlog source="*PowerShell/Operational" EventCode=4104 "whoami"
| table _time host Message


```comment
SEARCH A-BROAD (UNTESTED): also catches pwsh.exe and abbreviated flags (-e, -ec, -en...).
Expect more noise; review before alerting on it.
```
index=sysmon EventCode=1 (Image="*\\powershell.exe" OR Image="*\\pwsh.exe") (CommandLine="* -e *" OR CommandLine="* -ec *" OR CommandLine="* -en*")
| table _time host User ParentImage CommandLine
